Data licence — Open Food Facts
==============================

This repository imports product data from Open Food Facts (https://openfoodfacts.org).

That data is made available under the Open Database License (ODbL) v1.0:
    https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/

Individual contents of the database are under the Database Contents License (DbCL) v1.0:
    https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/dbcl/1-0/

Product images (not used by this importer) are under CC BY-SA.


What this obliges FamCart to do
-------------------------------

1. ATTRIBUTION (ODbL §4.3). Any public use of the derived data must credit Open Food Facts.
   FamCart discharges this with a user-visible line in the app's settings/about screen:

       Product data from Open Food Facts, © contributors, ODbL 1.0

   This is a required deliverable shipping WITH the first import, not a follow-up.

2. SHARE-ALIKE (ODbL §4.4). A publicly used Derivative Database must itself be offered under
   ODbL. This binds the DATA, not FamCart's application code — the two are separate works and
   coexist. The practical consequence is that the imported rows may not be relicensed under
   FamCart's own terms.

3. TRACEABILITY. Every imported row carries source = 'openfoodfacts' in product_catalog
   (migration 028). That column is what makes "which rows are ODbL" an answerable question, and
   it is the strongest reason the column exists. Rows that are curated or family-contributed are
   FamCart's own and carry no upstream obligation.


Note: this is a summary written to make the obligations actionable, not legal advice. Read the
licence text and Open Food Facts' terms of use before any commercial release.
